source: crates/aidp-cli/tests/cli_surface.rs
expression: normalized
---
The resident control plane: headless claude sessions, automations (cron / webhook / event), HTTP API + SSE for the viewer

Usage: <BIN> gateway [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  serve        Run the gateway daemon (sessions, automations, HTTP API + SSE)
  status       Daemon status: sessions, automations, rate-limit windows
  sessions     List sessions
  start        Start a session: a pipeline (`--template`, `--target`) or a free prompt (`--prompt`)
  reply        Send free text to a running session (gate answers go through the viewer)
  cancel       Cancel a running session
  automations  Manage automations
  projects     Manage the project registry the gateway launches sessions in
  presets      Manage launch presets
  queue        Inspect and steer the per-project launch queue
  worktrees    Inspect and prune the per-ticket git worktrees
  dispatcher   Manage the ticket-autopilot dispatcher (lot 9a): the resident loop that turns `todo` tickets into running sessions
  events       Recent gateway events
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
